      "value": "@{65f4b1a3d0a7a0c657a7d3a8|full_name} So I found the issue. It's due to my container being 90 degrees offset on the x-axis, causing the rotation constraint to do a gimbal rotation around the z-axis instead of being locked to it. I replicated it using Unity's rotation constraint by turning off the main object's parent constraint (which I removed from the upgrade since I didn't need those for freezing to the world anymore), which used a 0-degree offset. So, by using the solve using local space actually fixed it by taking account of the 90 degrees offset and using the world transform correctly.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
